    "turn_text": "This is the Cater daily podcast for Friday, March 7, 2025. I'm Caleb Brown. Trade is good. It advances prosperity. The tariffs pushed by the new administration, however, will be a disaster. According to U.S. Senator Rand Paul of Kentucky, as to his own branch of government, Congress, all the problematic spending pointed out by the so-called Department of Government Efficiency, without Congress, won't amount to much. We spoke on Wednesday. So I'm speaking to you from central Kentucky, and with respect to the new tariffs and threats of further tariffs, I thought about Toyota, a Japanese company that makes a lot of automobiles in Kentucky, Martin Raya, has big facilities in Kentucky as well, and to say nothing of the exports that Kentucky engages in. What have you heard from businesses in the Commonwealth about the impact that these tariffs are going to have on them?",
