    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, Elon Musk and Doge are doing great things. They're pointing out a lot of the things that I pointed out for a decade or more, but he has a bigger microphone and the world's attention is drawn to some of the craziness, particularly of foreign aid. You know, instinctively, most Americans are like, why are we sending money to foreign countries anyway? But then they find out it's like we're sending money for sex changes in Guatemala, for trans comic books in Peru, trans orchestras and operas in Colombia. uh three million dollars for girl centric climate change discussion in brazil just all kinds of insanity and people are rightly annoyed by it and they wanted to go away and they think elon has eliminated it and i just came from a meeting with him and my question to him was you're doing great stuff but it's not real unless we actually have it sent back to congress and be approved Now some of the administration just say, we'll just impound it. We won't spend it, and it'll somehow accrue back to the Treasury. But the Supreme Court ruled today, actually, that in all likelihood, the foreign aid needs to be spent because Congress told them to do it. The other thing we have going on is we're getting ready to do a spending bill in about two weeks in that spending bill, foreign aid is going to be spent at the same pace as it was last year. So for all the good stuff we're hearing, the actual spending is in changing. So it's a slide of hand. I want to make the spending cuts that Elon Musk is finding permanent and my admonition to him and to the administration is, send us a rescission package. A rescission package is a special bill that the administration says, we did what you told us, but we have leftover money because we were so efficient at it. We got rid of waste, fraud, and abuse, and here's a hundred billion dollars. has privilege, which means it has to be voted on, and the filibuster is not applicable. So it evades the filibuster by simple majority we can cut spending. So I'm advocating they send as much as they can. I'd look at a $500 billion decision package and say, let's vote and let's pass it. The question is whether or not we get enough Republicans. There are no Democrats in that. I don't say this to be mean, but there are no Democrats that will vote to cut spending. The question is, can we get to 50 Republicans or 51 Republicans that will vote to cut spending? That's an open question. But I think Trump should use some of his victory and his newfound power with public will to persuade the Republicans that, yes, we do need to vote for spending cuts. then what Elon's doing will be made permanent.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
