    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "Penny plan began the six penny plan this year. It was when we first started, you could actually do a freeze of spending for five years in balance of budget. Then it was the penny plan. And then after the penny plan, I think it became the three penny plan. Then COVID came and the Congress spent money like drunken sailors and now it's the six penny plan. It's an indication and the reason why I keep trying to stick with five years is I think getting beyond five years isn't even believable and even five years is a long time to wait. But that's what it takes a six percent cut each year for five years would get you to balance. But what we're talking about in two weeks amidst all The finding of waste by Elon Musk is they're talking about spending the same amount come March 14th, a continuing resolution without changes in spending to",
