    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "I'm not sure I would describe Doge as not being interested in the drivers of debt. I think they truly are. I mean, one of the things Elon Musk has talked about, the president talked about his speech last night, that's sending checks to dead people. I've said for years, couldn't we just all agree not to send money to dead people? That seems like a pretty easy compromise. I think they are looking at ways to audit the Pentagon. Some of his are sort of changing the way things are accounted for, you know, to make them eligible for an audit. And it's stuff that, you know, doesn't interest me as much, but it probably is important having each spending item itemized and it goes someplace and having someone responsible where you call someone up and says, this says you wrote a 10 million dollar check for X, what was X? You know, and so I think that I think everything Musk is doing is good. I just want to codify it. It isn't that I object to what he's doing or think it's insignificant. I think it actually is significant. I just want it to be real by making it or having Congress approve of it.",
